From: liuqin Fedora adaptation <liuqin@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] liuqin 7.3.1: battmgr-nowake

4320cc40; also cover the project-specific pen supply.
Original-Author: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Upstream-commit: https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin/commit/4320cc40084ae5754cb98ca90af9e744ae522894
Link: https://github.com/kettlelinux/kettlelinux/commit/6f00c5e5b457b95d69137b0c086de0785c6e7b52
Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Linux-derived code retains original GPL notices. Offline port; no hardware claim.
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -2727,6 +2727,7 @@
 	struct power_supply_config cfg = {
 		.drv_data = battmgr,
 		.fwnode = dev_fwnode(battmgr->dev),
+		.no_wakeup_source = true,
 	};
 
 	if (battmgr->pen_psy)
@@ -2793,6 +2794,10 @@
 	psy_cfg_supply.fwnode = dev_fwnode(&adev->dev);
 	psy_cfg_supply.supplied_to = qcom_battmgr_battery;
 	psy_cfg_supply.num_supplicants = 1;
+
+	/* Status updates must not turn every firmware message into a wakeup. */
+	psy_cfg.no_wakeup_source = true;
+	psy_cfg_supply.no_wakeup_source = true;
 
 	mutex_init(&battmgr->lock);
 	init_completion(&battmgr->ack);
